course: dictionary
lesson: 14319
title: Oblique: slanting, and not said plainly
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Oblique is a word with two main meanings. The first is about shape and direction: something that is oblique is slanting, not straight up and down and not flat. «The ladder leaned against the wall at an oblique angle.» The ladder is not upright, and it is not lying on the ground, so the clue is the word angle.
explain: The second meaning is about talking. An oblique remark does not say what it means plainly. It hints. «Dad gave an oblique hint about my birthday present, but he never said the word gift.» Dad was not clear, so you have to work out what he meant. Ask yourself: what is the plain meaning he is leaving out?
explain: In maths, oblique describes lines that meet at an angle that is not a right angle, like the corner of a square. Use the clues in the sentence to check: if the words around it talk about slanting or angles, the meaning is about direction; if they talk about hints or a reply, the meaning is about indirect speech.
fact: Oblique means slanting, at an angle, not straight up and not flat.
fact: In maths, an oblique line meets another line at an angle that is not a right angle.
fact: An oblique remark is an indirect hint, not a plain statement.
fact: In the UK, an oblique is the slash sign /, as in «and/or».
fact: Oblique is an adjective, so it describes a noun: an oblique line, an oblique hint, an oblique view.
exercise: «The ladder leaned against the wall at an oblique angle.» What does oblique mean here? | *Slanting, not straight up | Flat on the ground | Straight and upright | Very tall and thin
exercise: In maths, an oblique line meets another line at what kind of angle? | *An angle that is not a right angle | No angle at all | A tiny dot | A right angle, like the corner of a square
exercise: «Dad gave an oblique hint about my present.» What does oblique suggest about how Dad spoke? | He spoke very clearly | He wrote a long letter | He shouted the whole plan | *He hinted, without saying it plainly
test: «The rain fell in oblique streaks across the window.» What does oblique mean? | Very fast | Straight down | *Slanting, at an angle | Flat along the ground
test: Ella says, «Her reply was oblique, so I had to guess what she meant.» What does oblique tell you about the reply? | It was very long | It was written in another language | It was loud and clear | *It hinted at the meaning instead of saying it plainly
exam: In the UK, what is the sign called in «and/or»? | *An oblique | A full stop | A dash | A hyphen
